{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518576306,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTY5NTgyNTQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2166","origin":"github"},"title":"Generalize extractors into larger domains? meta-extractors?","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nwith autodetection of metadata types disabled imho it would be somewhat silly to generate and require specification of an extractor for each filetype in neuroimaging. So I wondered if nifti1 could/should be generalized into a more generic `neuroimaging_files`  or alike, which would provide extractors for other relevant datatypes ('.mgz', '.HEAD/.BRIK', etc) some of which are already supported by nibabel -- so it might be just a matter of a few additional dictionaries to define term mappins.\n\nWe could actually may be make 'meta-extractors' which provide such aggregation of different domain-specific ones.   I would just hate to go through each dataset and see which file types are in there... with every crawl/commit.  So I could just specify a set of domains for which to enable extractors for, in case they find some relevant file.","files":null}]}